---
import AutomaticPocketLayout from "../../layouts/AutomaticPocketLayout.astro";
import SupportEmail from "../../components/SupportEmail.astro";
---

<AutomaticPocketLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="Automatic Pocket collects no data. Audio is analysed on your device and never sent anywhere."
>
  <p class="label">Effective October 29, 2026</p>

  <p>
    Automatic Pocket doesn't collect, send or sell any information about you. There's no account,
    no ads, no analytics and no tracking, and the app doesn't connect to the internet.
  </p>

  <h2>The microphone</h2>
  <p>
    The app uses the microphone only while a session, a mic check or a calibration is running, to
    hear the notes you play or the calibration clicks. The sound is analysed on your device as it
    comes in. It isn't sent anywhere, and it isn't saved unless you turn on session recordings.
  </p>

  <h2>Session recordings</h2>
  <p>
    Recordings are off unless you turn on Keep session recordings in Audio setup. When it's on, the
    app saves what the mic heard during each session and how it scored it, on your device only. It
    keeps the last 20 and deletes older ones. A recording leaves your device only if you share it
    yourself from the results screen.
  </p>

  <h2>Your history and settings</h2>
  <p>
    Your scores, settings and headphone calibrations are stored on your device. Like other app data,
    they're included in your device's backups to iCloud or your computer, which Apple's privacy
    policy covers. Deleting the app deletes them.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>The app collects nothing from anyone, children included.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If this policy changes, the new version will be posted here with a new effective date.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Andrew Giffen, Toronto. Email <SupportEmail />.</p>
</AutomaticPocketLayout>
